# Runtime state NEVER lives in this repo. Everything the driver writes goes to
# $HOME/.mac-bootstrap/ — receipt.json, receipt.verify.json, bootstrap.log, rows/,
# backups/, and the fetched copies of the modules. These rules exist so that a stray
# copy in a working tree can never be committed.
receipt.json
receipt.verify.json
bootstrap.log
/rows/
/backups/

# Backups and half-written files made by the one settings writer.
*.mac-bootstrap-backup.*
*.mac-bootstrap-tmp.*
*.part

# Anything that would carry this machine's specifics into a public repo.
*.local
.env
.env.*
secrets.*

# macOS and editors.
.DS_Store
._*
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~

# Agent session state written INTO a working tree by the agent's own hooks. On this
# repo that is a publish hazard, not a nuisance: the task mirror is a render of the
# authoring machine's private task store and carries internal paths, session ids and
# third-party project names. It is regenerated at every session start, so deleting it
# once is not enough — it must never be committable. The canonical store lives under
# the agent config dir, so ignoring these loses nothing.
.claude-tasks/
.claude-plans/
.claude/settings.local.json

# diagram render toolchain
node_modules/
